/-!
# Derived global sections and derived completion

Let `A` be a ring, `I ⊂ A` a finitely generated ideal, `𝒞` a site, `𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras
on `𝒞` and `ℱ` a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules. [Stacks, Tag 0BLX] asserts the identity
`RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧)` in `D(A)` — the completion on the left along `I`, the one on the
right along `I𝒪` — and that it produces two spectral sequences,
```
E₂^{i,j} = H^i(H^j(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)   and   E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧)),
```
both converging to `H^*(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧) = H^*(𝒞, ℱ^∧)`.

This file sets up `A`-linear derived global sections on a ringed site, which the library did not
have, and proves the first spectral sequence, together with the second one at an assumed bounded
below representative of `ℱ^∧`. Neither statement here is the whole tag, and neither carries its
attribute: the identity is proved in `GlobalSectionsCompletionKoszulIdentity.lean`, and all three
assertions together, at the source's own hypotheses, are
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_and_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionWhole.lean`; see "How Tag 0BLX is completed" below.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionMulEnd`: multiplication by a global section of `𝒪`,
  as a ring homomorphism from `Γ(𝒞, 𝒪)` to the endomorphisms of the free rank-one module `𝒪`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleGlobalSectionsOver`: `Γ(𝒞, -)` as an additive functor
  `Mod(𝒪) ⥤ ModuleCat A`, for `𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOver`: `RΓ(𝒞, -) : D⁺(𝒪) ⥤ D⁺(A)`, its
  right derived functor.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.siteCohomologyOver`: `H^j(𝒞, -) = R^jΓ(𝒞, -)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj`: `RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)` read in the unbounded
  `D(A)`, which is where its derived completion along `I` lives.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy`: the property of being the ideal sheaf
  `I𝒪` generated by an ideal of the base ring.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_spectralSequence_derivedCompletion_globalSections`:
  the first spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX], `E₂^{i,j} = H^i(H^j(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)`
  converging to `H^{i+j}(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)`, with every term a derived complete `A`-module.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections`:
  the second spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX], `E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧))`
  abutting to `H^{p+q}(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧))`, at a bounded below representative of `ℱ^∧` and with
  [Stacks, Tag 099F] taken as an instance argument.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy`: the ideal sheaf `I𝒪` is
  determined by being generated by the global sections coming from `I`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.moduleGlobalSectionsOverEquivSections` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.smul_moduleGlobalSectionsOver`: `Γ(𝒞, -)` really is global
  sections, with the `A`-action prescribed by `ρ`.

## Implementation notes

*The `A`-algebra structure.* A sheaf of `A`-algebras is a sheaf of rings `𝒪` together with a
ring map `A ⟶ Γ(𝒞, 𝒪)`, and that is the data carried here: `ρ : A →+* Γ(𝒞, 𝒪)`, with
`Γ(𝒞, 𝒪) = RingCat.sectionsSubring 𝒪` the ring of compatible families of local sections.
Nothing stronger is assumed; in particular no terminal object of `𝒞` is required, so a global
section is a compatible family rather than a section over a final object.

*`A`-linear global sections.* `Γ(𝒞, ℱ)` is realized as `Hom_𝒪(𝒪, ℱ)`, that is as
`CategoryTheory.preadditiveCoyonedaObj` at the free rank-one module `SheafOfModules.unit`, whose
value is an `End(𝒪)ᵐᵒᵖ`-module; restriction of scalars along `globalSectionMulEnd` then makes it
an `A`-module. This route is taken rather than equipping the type `ℱ.sections` with an
`A`-action because additivity, which is what the derived functor machinery needs, is then
Mathlib's `CategoryTheory.additive_coyonedaObj`. The ring map `Γ(𝒞, 𝒪) ⟶ End(𝒪)` is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd` evaluated at `𝒪`, i.e. multiplication by the section;
it lands in the opposite ring because that is the side on which `End` acts on a `Hom`-group out
of `𝒪`, and multiplicativity holds in either order because the rings of sections of `𝒪` are
commutative.

*Derived global sections.* `D⁺` rather than `D`: `Mod(𝒪)` has enough injectives
([Stacks, Tag 01DU], `Stacks.Injectives.sheafOfModules_hasFunctorialInjectiveEmbeddings`), so
`RΓ` is everywhere defined on `D⁺` and `H^j(𝒞, -) = R^jΓ(𝒞, -)` by [Stacks, Tag 015A]; the
source's `RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)` for a *sheaf* `ℱ` is a bounded below object, so nothing of Tag 0BLX is lost.
`derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj` pushes it into the unbounded `D(A)` along
`DerivedCategory.Plus.ι`, which is where the derived completion of [Stacks, Tag 0BKE] acts;
`DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor` is *defined* as `Plus.ι ⋙ homologyFunctor`, so
`H^j(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ))` read in `D(A)` is `H^j(𝒞, ℱ)` on the nose — that is
`homologyFunctor_derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj`, which holds by `rfl`.

*The ideal sheaf `I𝒪`.* The library has no construction of the ideal sheaf generated by an ideal
of a base ring on a site (only `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ofIdealTop` for a
scheme). Rather than build one, `IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy` names the defining property — contains
every global section coming from `I`, and is least among the ideal sheaves that do — and
`eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy` shows it determines the ideal sheaf uniquely. A statement
carrying this hypothesis is therefore a statement about `I𝒪` and about nothing else.

### How Tag 0BLX is completed

The identity `RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧ = RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧)` is not proved in this file. The source proves it in one
line, by applying [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] to the morphism of ringed topoi `(𝒞, 𝒪) ⟶ (pt, A)`, and that
route is not the one taken: there is no morphism of ringed sites or ringed topoi from a general
ringed site to the ringed point in this library (what exists,
`Stacks.Sheaves.RingedPoint.RingedPointSituation.toRingedToposHom`, points the other way).

The identity is instead proved through the Koszul formula [Stacks, Tag 0A0E], which presents both
completions as derived limits of one Koszul tower: that is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedCompletion_derivedGlobalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionKoszulIdentity.lean`, at an arbitrary object of `D(𝒪)` and with no
hypothesis beyond the source's. The two inputs the second spectral sequence below takes —
[Stacks, Tag 099F] and a bounded below representative of `ℱ^∧` — are both produced at the
source's `I𝒪` in `GlobalSectionsCompletionGenerated.lean`. The whole tag is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_and_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionWhole.lean`, which carries the `@[stacks 0BLX]` attribute.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 015A](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/015A)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 015J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/015J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01DU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01DU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0G](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0G)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BKE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BKE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0BLX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0BLX)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open scoped IsMulCommutative

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

section Sections

variable (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})

/-- The rings of sections of the structure sheaf of a ringed site are commutative: the structure
sheaf takes values in `CommRingCat`, and `ringSheaf` only forgets the commutativity. -/
instance isMulCommutative_ringSheaf_obj (U : X.Cᵒᵖ) :
    IsMulCommutative (((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) := by
  change IsMulCommutative (X.O.obj.obj U); infer_instance

/-- Multiplication by a global section of `𝒪`, as an endomorphism of the free rank-one sheaf of
modules `𝒪`. This is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd`, which multiplies on every sheaf
of modules, evaluated at `SheafOfModules.unit`.

The target is the *opposite* ring of `End(𝒪)`, because that is the ring acting on the
`Hom`-groups out of `𝒪` in `CategoryTheory.preadditiveCoyonedaObj`. Multiplicativity holds in
either order, the rings of sections of `𝒪` being commutative. -/
@[sga "4 IV 11.1.3" "special case"]
def globalSectionMulEnd :
    RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj →+*
      (End (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))ᵐᵒᵖ where
  toFun s := MulOpposite.op <| End.of
    ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
        ⟨s.1, s.2⟩).asHom.app
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))
  map_one' := by
    refine congrArg MulOpposite.op (End.ext ?_)
    change (_ : SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⟶ _) = _
    ext U
    change (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) •
        (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) = _
    simp; rfl
  map_mul' s t := by
    refine congrArg MulOpposite.op (End.ext ?_)
    change (_ : SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⟶ _) = _
    ext U
    change (s.1 U * t.1 U) • (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) =
      t.1 U • (s.1 U • (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U))
    rw [← mul_smul]
    exact congrArg (fun r ↦ r • (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U))
        (mul_comm _ _)
  map_zero' := by
    refine congrArg MulOpposite.op (End.ext ?_)
    change (_ : SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⟶ _) = _
    ext U
    change (0 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) •
        (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) = _
    rw [zero_smul]; rfl
  map_add' s t := by
    refine congrArg MulOpposite.op (End.ext ?_)
    change (_ : SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⟶ _) = _
    ext U
    change (s.1 U + t.1 U) • (1 : ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj.obj U) = _
    rw [add_smul]; rfl

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A]
  (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)

/-- **`A`-linear global sections on a ringed site.** For `𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras, given by a
ring map `ρ : A ⟶ Γ(𝒞, 𝒪)`, this is `Γ(𝒞, -) : Mod(𝒪) ⥤ ModuleCat A`, realized as
`Hom_𝒪(𝒪, -)` with `A` acting through multiplication by global sections of `𝒪`. -/
def moduleGlobalSectionsOver :
    SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A :=
  preadditiveCoyonedaObj (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ⋙
    ModuleCat.restrictScalars ((globalSectionMulEnd X).comp ρ)

instance moduleGlobalSectionsOver_additive :
    (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).Additive :=
  inferInstanceAs
      (preadditiveCoyonedaObj (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ⋙
    ModuleCat.restrictScalars ((globalSectionMulEnd X).comp ρ)).Additive

/-- The underlying `A`-module of `Γ(𝒞, ℱ)` is the module of sections of `ℱ`: a map `𝒪 ⟶ ℱ` is
the same thing as a global section of `ℱ`, by `SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv`. Together with
`smul_moduleGlobalSectionsOver` this says `moduleGlobalSectionsOver` is global sections with the
`A`-action coming from `ρ`, and nothing else. -/
def moduleGlobalSectionsOverEquivSections
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).obj F ≃ F.sections :=
  F.unitHomEquiv

/-- `a : A` acts on `Γ(𝒞, ℱ) = Hom_𝒪(𝒪, ℱ)` by precomposition with multiplication by the global
section `ρ a` of `𝒪`; by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd_apply` that endomorphism is
scalar multiplication by `(ρ a)|_U` on sections over `U`. So the `A`-module structure is the one
`ρ` prescribes. -/
theorem smul_moduleGlobalSectionsOver
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) (a : A)
    (s : (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).obj F) :
    (a • s : (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).obj F) =
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.globalSectionToEnd ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))
          ⟨(ρ a).1, (ρ a).2⟩).asHom.app
          (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ≫
        (s : SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⟶ F) :=
  rfl

/-- **`RΓ(𝒞, -) : D⁺(𝒪) ⥤ D⁺(A)`**, the right derived functor of `A`-linear global sections.
Everywhere defined because `Mod(𝒪)` has enough injectives. -/
def derivedGlobalSectionsOver :
    DerivedCategory.Plus (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ⥤
      DerivedCategory.Plus (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
  (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).rightDerivedFunctorPlus

/-- **`H^j(𝒞, -) = R^jΓ(𝒞, -)`**, the cohomology of the site with coefficients in a sheaf of
`𝒪`-modules, as an `A`-module. This is [Stacks, Tag 015A] for `A`-linear global sections. -/
def siteCohomologyOver (j : ℤ) :
    SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)) ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} A :=
  (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).rightDerivedPlus j

/-- `RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)` read in the unbounded derived category `D(A)`, which is where its derived
completion along an ideal of `A` lives. -/
def derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) :=
  DerivedCategory.Plus.ι.obj ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).obj
    ((DerivedCategory.Plus.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F))

/-- The cohomology of `RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)`, computed in `D(A)`, is the cohomology of the site:
`DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor` is by definition `Plus.ι ⋙ homologyFunctor`, and
`R^jΓ` is by definition `H^j ∘ RΓ` applied to `ℱ` in degree zero. -/
theorem homologyFunctor_derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) (j : ℤ) :
    (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) j).obj
        (derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj X A ρ F) =
      (siteCohomologyOver X A ρ j).obj F :=
  rfl

end Sections

section FirstSpectralSequence

/-- **The first spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX].** Let `A` be a ring, `I ⊂ A` a finitely
generated ideal, `𝒞` a site, `𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras and `ℱ` a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules. There
is a bounded cohomological spectral sequence of derived complete `A`-modules with
```
E₂^{i,j} = H^i(H^j(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)
```
converging to `H^{i+j}(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)`, the completions being the derived completions along `I`.

Convergence is recorded as the source states it: a finite decreasing filtration of each
`H^n(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)^∧)`, exhaustive and separated, whose graded pieces are the eventual values of the
pages. The derived completion functor on `D(A)` is produced rather than assumed, its existence
([Stacks, Tag 0920]) being part of [Stacks, Tag 0BKE].

This is Tag 0BKE applied to `RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)`, as in the source, the identification of `H^j` of
`RΓ(𝒞, ℱ)` with `H^j(𝒞, ℱ)` being `homologyFunctor_derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj`.

This is one part of the tag and carries no `@[stacks 0BLX]` attribute: the whole lemma, at the
source's own hypotheses, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_and_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionWhole.lean`, which is registered. -/
theorem exists_spectralSequence_derivedCompletion_globalSections
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (hI : I.FG)
    (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
    (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) :
    let P : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A)) :=
      fun L ↦ _root_.IsDerivedComplete I L
    ∃ (completion : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} A) ⥤ P.FullSubcategory)
      (M : CochainComplex.Filtered (ModuleCat.{u} A))
      (E : E₂CohomologicalSpectralSequence (ModuleCat.{u} A))
      (hF : ∀ n : ℤ, Antitone (M.inducedFiltrationStep n)),
      Nonempty (completion ⊣ P.ι) ∧
      Nonempty (DerivedCategory.Q.obj M.X ≅
        (completion ⋙ P.ι).obj (derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj X A ρ F)) ∧
      (∀ n : ℤ, Nonempty (M.X.homology n ≅
        (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) n).obj
          ((completion ⋙ P.ι).obj (derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj X A ρ F)))) ∧
      (∀ i j : ℤ, Nonempty ((E.page 2).X (i, j) ≅
        (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) i).obj
          ((completion ⋙ P.ι).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) 0).obj
              ((siteCohomologyOver X A ρ j).obj F))))) ∧
      (∀ (r i j : ℤ) (hr : 2 ≤ r),
        IsDerivedCompleteModule I ((E.page r hr).X (i, j))) ∧
      (∀ n : ℤ, {i : ℤ | ¬ IsZero ((E.page 2).X (i, n - i))}.Finite) ∧
      (∀ n : ℤ, ∃ a b : ℤ, a ≤ b ∧ M.inducedFiltrationStep n a = ⊤ ∧
        M.inducedFiltrationStep n b = ⊥) ∧
      ∀ i j : ℤ, ∃ (r₀ : ℤ) (hr₀ : 2 ≤ r₀), ∀ (r : ℤ) (hr : r₀ ≤ r),
        (E.page r (by omega)).d (i, j) (i + r, j - r + 1) = 0 ∧
        (E.page r (by omega)).d (i - r, j + r - 1) (i, j) = 0 ∧
        Nonempty ((E.page r (by omega)).X (i, j) ≅
          cokernel (Subobject.ofLE (M.inducedFiltrationStep (i + j) (-j + 1))
            (M.inducedFiltrationStep (i + j) (-j)) (hF (i + j) (by omega)))) := by
  obtain ⟨completion, adj, -, -, -, -, -, -, -, M, eTotal, eCohomology, E, -, -, -, e₂,
    -, hF, -, hEcomplete, -, -, hEfin, hFilt, -, hEconv⟩ :=
    AdicFilteredCompletion.exists_spectralSequence_derivedCompletion_homology A I hI
      (derivedGlobalSectionsOverObj X A ρ F)
  exact ⟨completion, M, E, hF, ⟨adj⟩, ⟨eTotal⟩, fun n ↦ ⟨eCohomology n⟩,
    fun i j ↦ ⟨e₂ i j⟩, hEcomplete, hEfin, hFilt, hEconv⟩

end FirstSpectralSequence

section IdealSheaf

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)

/-- **The ideal sheaf `I𝒪`**, characterized rather than constructed: an ideal sheaf `𝓘` of `𝒪` is
*generated by `I`* when it contains the local sections of every global section coming from `I`,
and is least among the ideal sheaves that do.

The library has no construction of the ideal sheaf generated by an ideal of a base ring on a
site, so this property is what pins the ideal along which `ℱ^∧` is formed in
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections`. It determines `𝓘`
uniquely, by `eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy`. -/
def IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy
    (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))) : Prop :=
  (∀ (a : A) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), a ∈ I → (ρ a).1 U ∈ 𝓘.toSubmodule.obj U) ∧
    ∀ 𝓙 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
        (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))),
      (∀ (a : A) (U : X.Cᵒᵖ), a ∈ I → (ρ a).1 U ∈ 𝓙.toSubmodule.obj U) → 𝓘 ≤ 𝓙

/-- The ideal sheaf generated by an ideal of the base ring is unique: two ideal sheaves with the
property each lie below the other. -/
theorem eq_of_isIdealSheafGeneratedBy
    {𝓘 𝓙 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
      (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))}
    (h𝓘 : IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ 𝓘) (h𝓙 : IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ 𝓙) :
    𝓘 = 𝓙 :=
  le_antisymm (h𝓘.2 𝓙 h𝓙.1) (h𝓙.2 𝓘 h𝓘.1)

end IdealSheaf

section SecondSpectralSequence

variable (A : Type u) [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A) (X : RingedSite.{u, u, u})
  (ρ : A →+* RingCat.sectionsSubring ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)).obj)
  (𝓘 : SheafOfModules.Submodule
    (SheafOfModules.unit ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))))

/-- **The second spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 0BLX], at a given representative of `ℱ^∧`.**
Let `A` be a ring, `I ⊂ A` a finitely
generated ideal, `𝒞` a site, `𝒪` a sheaf of `A`-algebras, `𝓘 = I𝒪` the ideal sheaf it generates
and `ℱ` a sheaf of `𝒪`-modules. Write `ℱ^∧` for the derived completion of `ℱ` along `I𝒪`. Given
a bounded below complex `K` representing `ℱ^∧` and a Cartan-Eilenberg resolution of it, the
second spectral sequence of [Stacks, Tag 015J] for `Γ(𝒞, -)` has
```
E₂^{p,q} = H^p(𝒞, H^q(ℱ^∧))
```
and abuts to `H^{p+q}(RΓ(𝒞, ℱ^∧))`, which is `H^{p+q}(𝒞, ℱ^∧)`.

Following the library's statement of Tag 015J, the pages are those of the double complex
`Γ(𝒞, -)` applied to the resolution, read through [Stacks, Tag 0130]: the iterated cohomology
`H^p_{II}(H^q_I(-))` is the `E₂`-page of the second filtration, and the cohomology of the total
complex is the common abutment. That a double complex with finitely many nonzero terms on each
antidiagonal gives a bounded, convergent spectral sequence is [Stacks, Tag 0132],
`CochainComplex.exists_cohomologicalSpectralSequence` and
`CochainComplex.Filtered.abutsTo_of_isDegreewiseFinite`.

The bounded below representative `K` of `ℱ^∧` and the instance [Stacks, Tag 099F] are hypotheses
of this statement. Both are proved at the source's `I𝒪`, a finitely generated `I`'s `I𝒪` being
generated by finitely many global sections of `𝒪`: the instance by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_generatedIdealSheaf` and the
representative by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_plus_derivedCompletion_generatedIdealSheaf_obj`, which is how
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections_generatedIdealSheaf`
and the whole tag discharge them.
The resolution is a hypothesis for the same reason Tag 015J takes one — its existence is
[Stacks, Tag 015I], `CochainComplex.exists_cartanEilenbergResolution`, available here because
`Mod(𝒪)` has enough injectives.

This is one part of the tag and carries no `@[stacks 0BLX]` attribute: the whole lemma, at the
source's own hypotheses, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_iso_and_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections` of
`GlobalSectionsCompletionWhole.lean`, which is registered. -/
theorem exists_pages_derivedCompletion_globalSections
    (hI : I.FG) (h𝓘 : IsIdealSheafGeneratedBy A I X ρ 𝓘)
    [(ObjectProperty.ι (RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u, u, u, u} X 𝓘)).IsRightAdjoint]
    (F : SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O)))
    (K : CochainComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) ℤ)
    (hK : CochainComplex.plus (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) K)
    (eK : DerivedCategory.Q.obj K ≅ (derivedCompletion X 𝓘).obj
      ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F))
    (Ires : K.CartanEilenbergResolution)
    [HomologicalComplex₂.HasTotal
      ((((moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).mapHomologicalComplex
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj Ires.bicomplex)
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)] :
    let L := (((moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).mapHomologicalComplex
      (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).obj Ires.bicomplex
    (∀ p q : ℤ, Nonempty ((L.homology q).homology p ≅
      (siteCohomologyOver X A ρ p).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
            (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) q).obj
          ((derivedCompletion X 𝓘).obj
            ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor
              (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) 0).obj F))))) ∧
    ∀ n : ℤ, Nonempty ((HomologicalComplex₂.total L (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).homology n ≅
      (DerivedCategory.Plus.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A) n).obj
        ((derivedGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ).obj (DerivedCategory.Plus.Q.obj ⟨K, hK⟩))) := by
  -- `hI` and `h𝓘` are hypotheses of the source statement rather than inputs of this
  -- derivation: `h𝓘` is what makes `𝓘` be `I𝒪`, and finite generation of `I` is what makes
  -- derived completion along it well behaved. Both are recorded; neither is consumed here.
  obtain ⟨-, -⟩ := hI
  obtain ⟨-, -⟩ := h𝓘
  obtain ⟨-, hE₂, hTot⟩ :=
    CochainComplex.CartanEilenbergResolution.exists_homologyIso_rightDerivedPlus
      (moduleGlobalSectionsOver X A ρ) hK Ires
  refine ⟨fun p q ↦ ?_, hTot⟩
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := hE₂ p q
  refine ⟨e ≪≫ (siteCohomologyOver X A ρ p).mapIso ?_⟩
  exact ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctorFactors
      (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) q).app K).symm ≪≫
    (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor
        (SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf X.O))) q).mapIso eK

end SecondSpectralSequence

